 			<p>Jo looked up and Jo looked down, then said slowly, with sudden color in her cheeks, “It may be vain and wrong to say it, but⁠—I’m afraid⁠—Laurie is getting too fond of me.”</p>
 			<p>“Then you don’t care for him in the way it is evident he begins to care for you?” and <abbr epub:type="z3998:name-title">Mrs.</abbr> March looked anxious as she put the question.</p>
